{"body":"## Business Context & Purpose\n\nThe artifact COB currently records *what* artifacts exist (by CID) and *where* to get them (locations), but says nothing about *who verified them*. A consumer fetching an artifact must trust that the single delegate who published the CID actually built it correctly. There is no way for other project delegates to independently confirm \"I built from this commit and got the same CID.\"\n\nThis is a supply-chain security gap. Reproducible builds only help if multiple parties actually attest to the result and consumers can check those attestations.\n\n**Who benefits:**\n- **Consumers**: Can enforce policies like \"only trust releases attested by N-of-M delegates\"\n- **Project delegates**: Can demonstrate build reproducibility and shared accountability\n- **Security tooling**: Can programmatically query attestation status to gate CI/CD pipelines\n\n## Expected Behavior/Outcome\n\n### Target workflow (3 delegates)\n\n1. **Alice** (release initiator): `create` → `add_artifact(cid, name)` → `add_location(cid, url)` → `attest(cid)`\n2. **Bob** (verifier + mirror): builds independently, verifies CID matches → `attest(cid)` → `add_location(cid, url)`\n3. **Carol** (verifier only): builds independently, verifies CID matches → `attest(cid)` (no mirror required)\n4. **Consumer**: checks that all 3 project delegates attest before trusting the release\n\n### Key properties\n- Attestation is independent from hosting — a delegate can attest without mirroring\n- Idempotent: attesting the same CID twice is a no-op\n- Attesting a CID that doesn't exist in the release is a silent no-op (consistent with `AddLocation`)\n- Any node can attest; threshold enforcement is the consumer's responsibility\n\n## Research Summary\n\n**Investigation Depth**: STANDARD\n**Confidence Level**: High\n\n### Key Findings\n- **Product & User Story**: Four user stories identified — attest, view attestations, check threshold, revoke attestation. MVP should cover attest + view + check; revoke can be a follow-up.\n- **Technical Plan**: Implementation follows existing COB patterns exactly. No new dependencies. ~16-20 hours estimated effort.\n- **Risk**: Low. BTreeSet for deterministic serialization, backward-compatible (empty set default), idempotent operations match existing patterns.\n\n## Implementation Approach\n\n### Core changes (src/lib.rs)\n\n1. Add `Attest { cid: Cid }` variant to `Action` enum\n2. Add `attestations: BTreeSet<NodeId>` field to `Artifact` struct\n3. Add match arm in `Release::action()` — insert node into attestations set if CID exists\n4. Add `attest()` to `Transaction<R>` and `ReleaseMut`\n5. Add `attestations()` and `is_attested_by()` accessors to `Artifact`\n\n### Display changes (src/display.rs)\n\n6. Add attestations field to display `Artifact` struct\n7. Include attestations in both JSON and pretty output\n\n### CLI changes (src/bin/rad-artifact.rs)\n\n8. Add `Attest` command struct with `oid` and `cid` positional args\n9. Add handler function and error type following existing patterns\n\n### Tests (src/lib.rs)\n\n10. Multi-delegate attestation (3 nodes attest, verify all recorded)\n11. Idempotent attestation (duplicate is no-op)\n12. Attest missing CID (silent no-op)\n13. Attestation persists through reload\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `Action::Attest { cid }` variant exists and is serializable\n- [ ] `Artifact` tracks attestations as `BTreeSet<NodeId>`\n- [ ] `artifact.attestations()` returns the set of attesting NodeIds\n- [ ] `artifact.is_attested_by(node)` returns bool\n- [ ] `release.attest(cid, &signer)` records the attestation\n- [ ] Attesting same CID twice from same node is idempotent\n- [ ] Attesting a non-existent CID is a silent no-op\n- [ ] `rad artifact attest <oid> <cid>` CLI command works\n- [ ] `rad artifact show` displays attestations in both JSON and pretty formats\n- [ ] Existing tests continue to pass (backward compatible)\n- [ ] New tests cover multi-delegate, idempotent, and missing-CID cases\n\n## Dependencies & Constraints\n\n- No new crate dependencies needed (`BTreeSet` is in std, serde support is built-in)\n- Backward compatible: existing COBs with no attestations deserialize with empty set\n- Follows existing patterns: idempotent ops, silent no-ops, node-scoped actions\n\n## Future Considerations (out of scope for this issue)\n\n- `RevokeAttestation { cid }` action for delegates to withdraw attestation\n- Attestation levels/weights (e.g., \"verified build\" vs \"reviewed code\")\n- Integration with delegate policy (e.g., requiring attestation from project delegates specifically)","type":"comment"}